<section class="sec" id="faq" style="background:#fff">
<div class="wrap">
<span class="eyebrow reveal">FAQ</span>
<h2 class="st reveal">The questions people actually <span class="serif">ask.</span></h2>
<p class="lede reveal">If yours isn't here, a counsellor answers it on a 20-minute call.</p>
<div class="faq-wrap">
<div class="acc reveal">
<details open=""><summary>Is Python really the right first language? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">For almost everyone, yes. Its syntax reads like structured English, errors are learnable, and it leads directly into web, data and AI careers. That breadth is why we teach it as its own foundation course.</div></details>
<details><summary>I tried learning to code before and gave up. How is this different? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Structure and accountability. Daily drills, live debugging with a mentor, and problems sized to build momentum. Most self-taught attempts die from isolation, not difficulty; the batch fixes that.</div></details>
<details><summary>What jobs can I get with only Python? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Junior developer, automation engineer and scripting-heavy support roles hire on core Python plus projects. Many graduates instead continue into Full Stack or Data tracks with fee credit, entering those at higher speed.</div></details>
<details><summary>Which certification does this course prepare me for? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">PCEP from the Python Institute, the recognised entry credential, with exam-style practice built in. The exam is booked with the institute and charged separately.</div></details>
<details><summary>How much practice time does this really need? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Around 8 hours weekly: sessions plus daily 30-45 minute drills. Programming is a motor skill; the schedule exists to protect that daily repetition.</div></details>
<details><summary>Do you teach AI coding tools or ban them? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">We teach them as a discipline: prompt, review, test, own. Banning AI produces unemployable graduates; unsupervised AI produces incapable ones. The middle path is the skill.</div></details>
<details><summary>Is it online or classroom, and is Malayalam support available? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">Both. In-person batches in Trivandrum, Kochi and Bengaluru, plus live online batches across Kerala and the GCC. Sessions are in clear English with Malayalam support.</div></details>
<details><summary>Do you guarantee a job after the course? <span class="plus">+</span></summary><div class="ab">No, and we will not pretend otherwise. We provide structured placement support and real introductions across 400+ partners, with support continuing six months after you finish.</div></details>
</div>
